  "payload_model": {
    "convention": "Global bytes count each outgoing payload once; do not add incoming bytes again. Metadata is current 32-bit ring traffic, not FP16 plaintext bytes.",
    "dense_product": "Six checked joint inputs: 6*(4*N + 32) = 24*N + 192 global bytes, excluding transport framing. Average per party = 6*N + 48 bytes.",
    "complementary_sparse_product": "Four checked joint inputs: 4*(4*N + 32) = 16*N + 128 global bytes; each party sends 4*N + 32 bytes.",
    "quadratic_square": "x*x does not have complementary component support in general, so the current implementation uses the dense six-joint product. Fixed-point rescaling, range handling and other operations add traffic.",
    "attachment_claim": "One ring element per output describes one joint-input payload or a different protocol convention; it does not describe current global Rep4 product traffic. A 30x GeLU traffic reduction is not established by these ReLU fixture results."
