  "polynomial_comparison_requirements": [
    "Compare the same model, activation, tensor shapes, quantization, input set and output-opening boundary; this fixture currently evaluates ReLU, not GeLU or SwiGLU.",
    "Specify coefficients, polynomial degree, fit interval and approximation target. Report maximum and RMS approximation error over that interval, tail frequency outside the interval, and behavior outside it.",
    "Measure fixed-point quantization and truncation error separately from polynomial approximation error. Prove accumulator bounds for every multiply and preserve the probabilistic truncation quarter-ring range contract.",
    "Compare end-to-end maximum logit and log-probability error against FP32 and FP16 baselines, plus task-level quality on representative held-out inputs; add perplexity or accuracy where appropriate.",
    "For probabilistic rounding use fresh randomness across repeated runs and report error distribution and worst observed errors; exact transcript replay only validates replay consistency.",
    "Benchmark a complete private polynomial activation with checked multiplication, required rescaling, fresh PRG draws, communication and final output checks. Count rounds and actual outgoing global bytes; do not substitute an arithmetic operation count for latency.",
    "Keep the same privacy/integrity threshold. No TEE or opening of activations is assumed in these scenarios."
